.TH JITTERENTROPY-FLAGS 1 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "User Commands"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jitterentropy-flags \- encode and decode the flags of the CPU Jitter RNG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jitterentropy-flags
.RB [ \-\-hex ]
.I flag
\&...
.br
.B jitterentropy-flags \-\-decode
.I value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jitterentropy-flags
converts between the
.B JENT_*
flags described in
.BR jitterentropy (3)
and the number a caller passes, such as
.B jitterentropy-rngd
with
.BR \-\-flags .
It knows the flags of the
.I jitterentropy.h
it was built with and runs no Jitter RNG.
.PP
Given flags, it prints their sum in decimal, or with
.B \-\-hex
in hexadecimal. A
.I flag
is a
.B JENT_*
name, case-insensitive and with the
.B JENT_
prefix optional, such as
.BR JENT_NTG1 ,
.B ntg1
or
.BR max_memsize_1mb ,
or an option of
.BR jitterentropy-rng ,
such as
.B \-\-force\-fips
or
.BI \-\-max\-mem " n",
which are matched by their prefix as there.
Setting the memory size or the hash loop field twice to different values is
an error.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-decode ,
it prints every flag and whether
.I value
sets it, followed by the reserved bits and the values of the hash loop and
memory size fields.
.I value
is decimal, or hexadecimal with a
.B 0x
prefix.
.B JENT_FORCE_SECURE_MEM
reads
.I implied
where
.B JENT_FORCE_FIPS
or
.B JENT_NTG1
imply it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 1 for an invalid argument, and for flags that
.BR jent_entropy_init_ex ()
and
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc ()
of
.BR jitterentropy (3)
refuse: a reserved bit, a field value above its maximum,
.B JENT_FORCE_INTERNAL_TIMER
with
.B JENT_DISABLE_INTERNAL_TIMER
or
.BR JENT_NTG1 ,
or
.B JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS
with
.B JENT_FORCE_FIPS
or
.BR JENT_NTG1 .
The number or the table is printed nonetheless, and the reasons go to
standard error. The system's FIPS mode, which refuses
.B JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS
as well, is not checked.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ jitterentropy-flags ntg1 JENT_MAX_MEMSIZE_1MB
1476395072
$ jitterentropy-flags --decode 0x58000040
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jitterentropy-hashtime (1),
.BR jitterentropy (3),
.BR jitterentropy-record (3)
